# CUA verify after finish

When a task changes **in-game / GUI / JEI / keybind** behavior (Forge or NeoForge Pack AI):

1. Finish code + log + compile/jar as usual.
2. **Then** use `user-cua-driver` to smoke-test (prefer existing `runClient` window; relaunch only if classpath stale).
3. Minimum checks when relevant: open Pack AI (`]`), see expected reply/cards/labels; screenshot under `dist/cua_*.png`.
4. OpenGL click calibration (Windows):
   - Fresh `get_window_state` immediately before every click (window may move).
   - Screenshot often includes ~30px title bar while client is shorter — don't aim by "guess mid-logo"; zoom the real button, then click.
   - Confirm SendInput screen coords land inside `GetWindowRect` (earlier miss used stale/wrong X far left of MC).
   - Prefer in-world / pause-menu once loaded; title ok if coords verified.
5. End CUA session when done. Report pass/fail briefly — do not skip CUA just because unit tests passed.
